                        "entry_id": "75afdb28-7404-34d7-b33e-78eefeaf5b05",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In violation of a moral or other standard, code, or convention; in an unfair, unjust, dishonest, or immoral manner; unfairly, unjustly, dishonestly, immorally, wrongfully; wrongly convicted is synonymous with wrongful conviction and miscarriage of justice."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "acbd9213-d628-3b54-a0a7-a0dee1377c61",
                        "entry_id": "75afdb28-7404-34d7-b33e-78eefeaf5b05",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Incorrectly, mistakenly; by error."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9841d5f-42f1-44e8-bf15-12f291796f5b",
                                "sense_id": "acbd9213-d628-3b54-a0a7-a0dee1377c61",
                                "text": "I wrongly assumed that it would be an easy job."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d51c684-c83f-4139-91a2-0687ad144896",
                                "sense_id": "acbd9213-d628-3b54-a0a7-a0dee1377c61",
                                "text": "\"The minute I put my nose in that door she was at me for a drop of gin, but having no instructions to supply it, and being strictly teetotal myself, I have not done so, whether rightly or wrongly I leave you to judge, doctor.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0559fed3-0a4c-4fdc-b6b4-ab074d29dff9",
                                "sense_id": "acbd9213-d628-3b54-a0a7-a0dee1377c61",
                                "text": "In March 2021, Mr. Livingston finally went up for parole after one of the lawyers from Appellate Advocates, De Nice Powell, argued he had been wrongly sentenced in the razor-blade contraband case and got the sentence reduced."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
